  "title": "High Credit Inquiry Velocity Emerges as Top Fraud Risk Indicator in Rental Applications",
  "summary": "Rental applicants with unusually high numbers of recent credit inquiries pose the greatest fraud risk for property managers, according to TransUnion (NYSE: TRU) research released today at Apartmentalize 2026. Applicants with 15 or more credit inquiries in the seven days prior to applying for a lease showed the highest rate of charge-offs within ...",
